<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Talamone</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Talamone is a small coastal village in southern Tuscany, in the comune of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orbetello">Orbetello</a>. Near it the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> destroyed a large Gallic army at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-telamon">Battle of Telamon</a> in 225 BCE. In the 16th century it was one of the fortresses of the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-the-presidi">State of the Presidi</a>, and in 1860 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-garibaldi">Garibaldi</a>'s Thousand stopped there on their way to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/talamone.jpg" alt="Talamone" width="320" height="124" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alessio Damato · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Talamone_panorama_top.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
